{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Shall be set alive.</b> Like 'shall be made to stand alive' — by the hands of others, and its Targum is יִתָּקַם כַּד חַי. What does the verse teach? Since it says 'to send him to Azazel,' and I do not know whether his sending is to death or to life, therefore it says 'shall be set alive' — his standing is alive until he is sent off. From here that his sending is to death (Sifra)." "<b>To make atonement upon it.</b> That he confess over it, as it is written ״וְהִתְוַדָּה עָלָיו״ etc."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:43.771954736Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}